### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO.______

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION ADOPTING THE 8TH AVENUE CORRIDOR PLAN”

WHEREAS, Eighth Avenue is situated between Lion’s Park, Frontier Park, the
Avenues and Moore Haven Heights neighborhoods; and

WHEREAS, the intersection of 8th Avenue and Carey Avenue is a skewed
intersection; functions as both a park access road and a bypass route for commuters traveling
between downtown and the north end of Cheyenne; and creates both operational and safety
concerns for vehicles, cyclists and pedestrians; and

WHEREAS, traffic from the neighborhood ranges from 500 vehicles a day on the
western end to 2,500 near Central Avenue.  During Frontier Days and major event days at
Lion’s Park, traffic can be as high as 10,000 vehicles a day or more; and

WHEREAS, in 2010, representatives of the neighborhood submitted a request to the
Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO) through the City’s Neighborhood
Traffic Management Program (NTMP) to review conditions on 8th Avenue and develop a set
of improvements that would enhance vehicle operations and improve pedestrian safety both
along and across the corridor; and

WHEREAS, the MPO initiated the 8th Avenue Corridor Plan in 2011 to develop
recommendations for the aforementioned problems and to create a vision for 8th Avenue; and

WHEREAS, The plan has been a collaborative effort involving the general public,
corridor stakeholders, the Wyoming Department of Transportation, Federal Highway
Administration, and the City of Cheyenne; and

WHEREAS, the Cheyenne MPO retained Felsburg, Holt and Ullevig on November 28,
2011 to produce the 8th Avenue Corridor Plan; and

WHEREAS, the 8th Avenue Corridor Plan recommends infrastructure improvements
that are intended to enhance pedestrian and bicycle safety along the corridor; provide safer
areas to cross the roadway; revise the roadway laneage to meet the everyday and event loading
needs of the corridor; and improve the 8th Avenue/Carey Avenue intersection to provide a
safer and more efficient intersection for vehicle, pedestrian and bicycle traffic; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission held a Public Meeting on
May 6, 2013, accepted public comments, and recommended that the Governing Body of the
City of Cheyenne approve the 8th Avenue Corridor Plan; and

WHEREAS, the Cheyenne MPO Citizen’s Advisory and Technical Committee
reviewed the Plan and recommended adoption; and
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
WHEREAS, the 8th Avenue Corridor Plan will be used for prioritization of future
transportation projects in the City.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF
THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING:

THAT, the 8th Avenue Corridor Plan dated May 2013, prepared by Felsburg, Holt and
Ullevig, is hereby approved as a guide for future improvements to the corridor.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED THIS ____ DAY OF ___________, 2013.

___________________________
Richard L. Kaysen, Mayor
City of Cheyenne

(Seal)

ATTEST:

____________________________
Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk
```
